🌐 API Responsibilities

The API layer handles:

Request creation
Response parsing
Authentication headers
HTTP errors
Network exceptions
Serialization
Retry-compatible failures

Business logic remains outside the Retrofit service layer.

💾 Local Database

Room is used as the local persistence abstraction.

Responsibilities:

Store operational data
Provide offline access
Support reactive queries
Persist synchronization state
Reduce unnecessary network dependency

Example:

@Dao
interface WorkOrderDao {


    @Query("SELECT * FROM work_orders")
    fun observeWorkOrders(): Flow<List<WorkOrderEntity>>


    @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
    suspend fun insertWorkOrders(
        items: List<WorkOrderEntity>
    )
}
⚙️ Background Processing

WorkManager is used for tasks that need reliable background execution.

Examples:

Data synchronization
Pending operation processing
Retry operations
Periodic refresh
Cleanup operations
🔐 Security

Security considerations include:

Secure API communication
Sensitive-data minimization
Secure credential handling
Android platform security mechanisms
Controlled local persistence
Avoiding secrets inside source code

Never commit:

API keys
Passwords
Private certificates
Production secrets
Service credentials
⚡ Performance

Performance considerations include:

Startup
Minimize unnecessary initialization
Lazy-load expensive dependencies
Avoid blocking main-thread operations
Database
Use indexed queries where appropriate
Avoid unnecessary database reads
Prefer reactive Room queries
UI
State-driven Compose UI
Avoid unnecessary recomposition
Stable UI models
Efficient list rendering
Networking
Request only required data
Use caching/local persistence
Avoid duplicate requests
